   "text": "I finished the review: the verdict is **NEEDS FIX (minor)**, with one consistency defect on 討. The report is written, read back once in full, and the two-line completion message has gone to the coordinator.\n\n**The defect:** 討's title is \"attack; discuss\", but its quiz exclusions don't cover 話 \"talk, speak\" or 争 \"contend; dispute\". It already excludes 談, 議 and 論 for the same \"discuss\" sense. In the full N1 and All pools the three hand-picked distractors fill every wrong slot, so this can't show up there. It could show up in custom pools and in the padded Starter session, because 話 is tagged `starter`. That Starter case comes from REVIEW.md and the tags; it wasn't run in the app. The suggested fix is to add 話 and 争 to 討's exclusions.\n\n**Everything else is CLEAN** for the 15 new cards, the 応/統 edits and the 30 backlinks. I compared each new card's metadata against the supplied KANJIDIC2 records, the Joyo table extract and the JMdict entries in the packet. The report also lists 12 optional points, such as 寧–和, and several exclusions that rest only on a shared English word (for example 隊–秒 \"unit\").\n\n**Not covered:**\n- The KanjiVG stroke drawings (segments 50–56) and the Joyo PDF weren't read, as instructed.\n- I made no web fetches, so claims sourced only from the Daijisen dictionary are unverified.\n- Some collision candidates beyond the 40/10 caps were judged from titles only. The report lists them under Limits.\n\n**Read record:** required segments 1–49 and extension segments 1–10, each read once, with no re-reads.\n\n**Typo:** one cell in the D/E table reads \"starter-tagged (種 none)\". The parenthetical is a stray fragment; the cell should just say 話 is starter-tagged. I couldn't correct it because only a single write was allowed.\n\nMy model is reported by the runtime as Claude Opus 5.5; I can't verify that from inside the run.\n\nReport: `C:\\Users\\stop-\\n1-kanji-workspace\\reports-113\\initial-claude-m5.md`"
  }
